.\" zvoltimeline(1) — manual page, mdoc. Kept true to the program by
.\" tests/man-check.sh.
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt ZVOLTIMELINE 1
.Os zvolrescue 0.9.8
.Sh NAME
.Nm zvoltimeline
.Nd the history of a ZFS pool from the transaction groups it still carries
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar dev ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads every transaction group (TXG) that still verifies on the members
of a pool, oldest to newest, and turns the differences between them
into a history: when each dataset, volume and snapshot was created,
renamed, destroyed or cloned, and what its properties were.
It reads the members the way
.Xr zvolrescue 1
does, never writes to them, and can write an evidence log the same
way.
.Pp
The pool members are given as devices, or as image files with
.Fl -image .
The
.Sx POOL MEMBER OPTIONS
and the global options are those of
.Xr zvolrescue 1
and are listed here in brief.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -from Ar txg
Oldest transaction group to read; default the oldest that verifies.
.It Fl -to Ar txg
Newest transaction group to read; default the newest that verifies.
.It Fl -dataset Ar name | guid
Only events about this object: a dataset name at any TXG, or a GUID.
.It Fl -pending
Also report how much space is held by things ZFS has finished with
but has not freed.
While a block is still accounted for there, it has not been
reallocated.
.It Fl o , Fl -output Ar file
Write the report to
.Ar file
instead of standard output.
.It Fl f , Fl -format Ar text | json
Output format; text is the default.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Increase verbosity; repeatable.
.It Fl q , Fl -quiet
Suppress non-essential output.
.It Fl -evidence-log Ar file
Append a JSON Lines evidence log to
.Ar file .
.It Fl -hash-inputs
Also record the SHA-256 of every input in the evidence log.
.It Fl -no-color
Disable colour in text output.
.It Fl -debug , Fl -debug-log Ar file
Trace every read decision, to standard error or to
.Ar file .
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh POOL MEMBER OPTIONS
As in
.Xr zvolrescue 1 :
.Fl -image Ar file
(an image file that is a member; repeatable),
.Fl -hints Ar file
(the layout by hand),
.Fl -search-order
(try every member order the layout leaves open),
.Fl -pool-guid Ar guid
(which pool when several are found),
.Fl -assume-member Ar path Ns Op = Ns Ar guid
(a member whose labels are gone),
.Fl -ignore-unknown-features ,
.Fl -map Ar member Ns = Ns Ar mapfile
(the ddrescue mapfile an image was made with),
.Fl -device-may-fail
and
.Fl -surface-scan-on-device .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
As in
.Xr zvolrescue 1 :
0 success, 1 usage, 2 evidence unreadable, 3 nothing readable, 5
refused, 7 the medium refused a read.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Everything the ring of two mirror members still tells, as JSON:
.Dl zvoltimeline -f json /dev/ada0p3 /dev/ada1p3
.Pp
What happened to one volume, with what its freed space still holds:
.Dl zvoltimeline --dataset pool/vm/disk0 --pending /dev/ada0p3 /dev/ada1p3
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zvolreport 1 ,
.Xr zvolrescue 1
